WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.554
Authentication establishes who the user or service is.

2
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:08.697
Authorization decides what that identity may read, write, request, or trigger.

3
00:00:08.697 --> 00:00:13.461
In AI applications, both remain ordinary application responsibilities.

4
00:00:13.461 --> 00:00:23.368
The model should not decide whether a user can access a document, retrieve a tenant's data, invoke a tool, or approve a workflow based only on generated text.

5
00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:31.536
Python code and identity systems should enforce those decisions before context is assembled and before actions are performed.

6
00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:35.091
Object-level authorization is especially important.

7
00:00:35.091 --> 00:00:42.653
A user may be allowed to use an assistant but not allowed to access every record the assistant can technically retrieve.

8
00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:53.392
Retrieval filters should include user identity, session context, tenant, organization, role, document classification, and resource ownership where appropriate.

9
00:00:53.392 --> 00:01:03.148
If the user could not access the object through the normal application, the AI path should not expose it through a summary, citation, answer, or tool call.

10
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:08.215
Data minimization and purpose limitation reduce both exposure and confusion.

11
00:01:08.215 --> 00:01:16.912
The application should send only the data needed for the approved task, and only for a purpose the user and organization have authorized.

12
00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:30.449
Secrets, credentials, private keys, tokens, source code, customer information, and regulated data should not be included in prompts or retrieved context unless the flow is explicitly approved and controlled.

13
00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:35.062
Retrieved content should never be allowed to expand what data it can see.

14
00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:38.087
Model output should not approve its own access.

15
00:01:38.087 --> 00:01:48.297
If the model says it needs a restricted document or a powerful tool, that request should go through the same authorization and approval path as any other request.

16
00:01:48.297 --> 00:01:52.002
This separation is the heart of prompt injection defense.

17
00:01:52.002 --> 00:02:01.682
The model may propose, explain, summarize, or ask for clarification, but the application decides what data is available and which actions are allowed.
